# STRICT RULE: Sanity CMS Scope (PRD v2.0)

**Exactly SIX villager document types exist, plus the supporting `category`.**
Do NOT add more document types without human approval.

## Allowed Document Types

| `_type` | Studio label | Body | Notes |
|---------|--------------|------|-------|
| `artikel_berita` | Berita | `blocks[]` (bilingual) | Only type with a `category` reference |
| `artikel_sejarah` | Sejarah | `blocks[]` (bilingual) | No category; fixed frontend label |
| `artikel_partnership` | Partnership | `blocks[]` (bilingual) | No category; fixed frontend label |
| `artikel_liputan` | Liputan | none | `externalUrl` + `sourceName`; NO detail page |
| `wisata` | Wisata | `description_id/en` (Portable Text) | Bilingual REQUIRED; native Sanity Draft/Publish; `gallery` ≤ 10 |
| `desa` | Desa | `description_id/en` (Portable Text) | Fixed `villageName` (gobleg/munduk/gesing/umejero); `dataFields[]`; `gallery` |
| `category` | Kategori | — | Referenced only by `artikel_berita` |

The three body-bearing article types share one factory:
`koneksi-cms/schemas/shared/createArticleType.ts` (bilingual `blocks[]` via
the `articleBlock` object + custom Studio components). Reuse it — do not
duplicate the fields.

## Supporting (non-document) types

`portableText` (array), `youtube` (object), `articleBlock` (object) — these are
NOT documents. Register everything in `koneksi-cms/schemas/index.ts` and wire
the desk in `koneksi-cms/sanity.config.ts` (Artikel → Berita / Sejarah /
Partnership / Liputan; Kategori nested under Berita only; then Wisata, Desa).

## Villager Permission Boundary

| Action | Allowed |
|--------|---------|
| Create/edit/publish the 4 article types | ✅ Yes |
| Edit wisata (Sanity Publish) | ✅ Yes |
| Edit the 4 desa documents | ✅ Yes (edit content) |
| Select/create `category` (kategori) | ✅ Yes |
| Create/delete extra desa or change `villageName` | ❌ NO (4 fixed) |
| Edit booklet / gallery / maps / downloads | ❌ NO (hardcoded) |
| Edit site settings / navigation / footer | ❌ NO (code only) |

## What Does NOT Go in Sanity

Hardcoded TypeScript data files instead (see `data-architecture` rule):
`data/booklet.ts`, `data/gallery.ts`, `data/maps.ts`, `data/downloads.ts`.
The Instagram feed comes from the Graph API, not Sanity.

## Migrations

Changing a document `_type` is not a patch operation. The legacy
`article → artikel_berita` conversion is a `sanity exec` script:
`koneksi-cms/scripts/migrate-article-to-berita.ts`
(`npm run migrate:article-to-berita`). Run once by the team.
